HHIISSTTOORRYY
       ppaammaarriitthh replaced ppnnmmaarriitthh in Netpbm 10.3 (June 2002).

       In Netpbm 10.3 through 10.8, though, ppaammaarriitthh was not backward compati‐
       ble  because  it  required the input images to be of the same depth, so
       you could not multiply a PBM by a PPM as is  often  done  for  masking.
       (It  was  not  intended at the time that ppnnmmaarriitthh would be removed from
       Netpbm -- the plan was just to rewrite it to use ppaammaarriitthh; it  was  re‐
       moved by mistake).

       But starting with Netpbm 10.9 (September 2002), ppaammaarriitthh allows the im‐
       ages to have different depths as long as one of them has depth  1,  and
       that made it backward compatible with ppnnmmaarriitthh.

       The original ppnnmmaarriitthh did not have the --mmeeaann option.

       The --ccoommppaarree option was added in Netpbm 10.13 (December 2002).

       The bit string operations were added in Netpbm 10.27 (March 2005).

       The --ddiivviiddee option was added in Netpbm 10.30 (October 2005).

       The  ability  to have more than one input (operand) was added in Netpbm
       10.93 (December 2020).

       The --eeqquuaall option was added in Netpbm 10.93 (December 2020).

